        "SIGNALMENT": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "SIGNALMENT",
          "canonical_heading": "SIGNALMENT",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Idiopathic—one study suggests male golden retrievers 4–13 years of age at increased risk. Most of these localize to a postganglionic",
              "pdf_page": 738,
              "printed_page": 656,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "lesion.",
              "pdf_page": 738,
              "printed_page": 656,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Idiopathic—50–93% of Horner’s syndrome in dogs; 45% in cats. Hypothalamus First order neuron Brainstem/cervical cord T3–L3 spinal cord segments and nerve roots Second order neuron/preganglionic Vagosympathetic trunk Cranial cervical ganglion Tympanic bulla Third order neuron/Ophthalmic branch of post-ganglionic trigeminal nerve Iris dilator muscles, periorbital smooth muscles, upper and 3rd eyelid Figure 1. Table 1 Summary of lesions resulting in Horner’s syndrome.",
              "pdf_page": 738,
              "printed_page": 656,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "subheading",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Lesion Location",
              "pdf_page": 738,
              "printed_page": 656,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "SIGNS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "SIGNS",
          "canonical_heading": "SIGNS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Miosis.",
              "pdf_page": 738,
              "printed_page": 656,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Protruding third eyelid.",
              "pdf_page": 738,
              "printed_page": 656,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Ptosis",
              "pdf_page": 738,
              "printed_page": 656,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "(drooping) of upper eyelid.",
              "pdf_page": 738,
              "printed_page": 656,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Enophthalmos.",
              "pdf_page": 738,
              "printed_page": 656,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Other neurologic and non-neurologic signs dependent on the underlying cause.",
              "pdf_page": 738,
              "printed_page": 656,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
        "CAUSES": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "CAUSES",
          "canonical_heading": "CAUSES",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Brainstem Neoplasia, encephalitis, vascular, trauma C1–T3 spinal cord IVDH, trauma, neoplasia, FCE T1–T3 nerve roots Brachial plexus avulsion, peripheral nerve tumor (lymphoma, nerve sheath tumor most common) Sympathetic trunk, Trauma, iatrogenic following cranial cervical jugular venipuncture, ganglion mediastinal or thyroid neoplasia Tympanic bulla Otitis media, polyp (cat), neoplasia, trauma Retrobulbar Neoplasia, abscess, trauma",
              "pdf_page": 738,
              "printed_page": 656,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
